  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.ContextPhase` is a declaration with no MUST, SHOULD or MAY clause. Its only concrete, testable obligation is that the SDK exports a public unit struct `ContextPhase`. Its prose says the type marks an agent request that can still accept context. That behaviour belongs to the refining requirements `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.agent_context` and `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.phases`, so it needs no test here. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#struct[ContextPhase]` carries an {impl} reference to `judge.phases`. The `context` method is implemented only on `impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, ContextPhase>]`.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` carries the {test} reference. It generates rustdoc for the SDK and compares the exported paths and item kinds with the inventory specified under `md/requirements/sdk`. The helpers it reaches are `specified_exports` and `documented_exports`. Rustdoc's item categories such as `struct` are matched with the inventory's declared kinds. The test asserts that nothing is missing or unexpected. Removing `ContextPhase`, making it private, or turning it into a different kind of item would therefore fail it. I found no gap.",
